<h2>What is excluded from these starting prices?</h2>
<p>To understand the <strong>Varanasi Ayodhya Prayagraj tour package cost</strong>, it is important to separate the ground programme from your complete holiday budget.</p>
<p>The starting prices above exclude:</p>
<ul><li>Hotel accommodation.</li><li>Meals.</li><li>Entrance fees.</li><li>Flights and rail tickets.</li><li>Personal expenses and tips.</li><li>Optional upgrades and additional experiences.</li></ul>
<p>Any service added to your confirmed quotation will be identified clearly.</p>
<p>Special darshan arrangements, personal pujas, priest services, donations and personal Sankalp rituals should be discussed individually. A temple visit in an itinerary does not, by itself, mean that every optional ritual or special-access arrangement is included.</p>
<h2>How much should you budget for hotels?</h2>
<p>Hotel choice can make a substantial difference to the total cost of a <strong>private Varanasi and Ayodhya tour</strong>.</p>
<p>Some travellers prefer practical hotels with easy vehicle access. Others want a heritage property, a riverside stay or a larger hotel with more facilities. Room category, occupancy, meal plan and travel dates also affect the quotation.</p>
<p>We quote hotels separately so that you can choose accommodation suited to your comfort and budget. If you have already booked your rooms, we can plan the ground services around those hotels.</p>
<p>When requesting hotel options, please mention the number of double, twin or triple rooms required, along with the ages of any children.</p>
<h2>Private sedan or Innova Crysta: which should you choose?</h2>
<p>The starting package prices use a <strong>private sedan</strong>. An Innova Crysta, Hycross, Urbania or larger vehicle can be quoted according to the number of guests and luggage requirements.</p>
<p>Vehicle choice should take account of the whole journey. A party travelling with large suitcases may need more luggage space even when the passenger count is small. Guests who find frequent boarding difficult may also have particular seating preferences.</p>
<p>For a <strong>Varanasi to Ayodhya tour by car</strong>, share the passenger count, luggage details and any mobility needs before confirming the vehicle. We can then recommend a suitable option and show the upgrade cost separately.</p>
